# Auto-requests review from the maintainer on every change.
#
# With one maintainer this does little today — it requests review from the
# person opening the PR. It is here so that adding a second contributor is
# a one-line change rather than a thing someone has to remember, and so
# security-sensitive paths carry an explicit owner from the start.
#
# This is routing, not a security control. It does not enforce review;
# branch protection does that.

